The task is complete. Here's what I implemented:

**New function: extract_error_source_context** — reads the actual source files referenced in compiler errors and extracts an 11-line window (±5 lines) around each error location. The function:
• Deduplicates (file, line) pairs so the same location only appears once
• Caps total injected context at 3KB (SOURCE_CONTEXT_MAX_BYTES) 
• Silently skips files that don't exist or can't be read
• Returns a formatted markdown section with file headers and line numbers

Modified: `build_watch_fix_prompt` — now calls the helper after parsing errors and appends the source context section to the fix prompt, so the fixing agent sees both the error output AND the relevant code in the same turn.

6 new tests:
1. Empty errors → empty result
2. Non-existent files → empty result (silent skip)
3. Errors without file field → empty result
4. Real file → correct window extraction with line numbers
5. Duplicate file+line → only included once
6. Many files with long lines → respects the 3KB cap
7. Integration: build_watch_fix_prompt includes source context when errors have file references
